INT. COMMUNITY POOL SNACK BAR - DAY

Chlorine haze. A hand-lettered menu. Rain drums the skylight and the pool outside is closed for the day.

BEATRIX LOMBARDI (40s, harried, whistle around her neck) wipes the counter. Her kids sit on stools: DESMOND (12, serious, goggles pushed up on his forehead) and little PIPPA (6, one flip-flop on).

BEATRIX
Who ate the last pretzel?

PIPPA
Not me.

DESMOND
She did. There's salt on her chin.

Pippa wipes her chin with her whole sleeve.

BEATRIX
Pippa.

PIPPA
It was a small pretzel.

NANA ROSALIND (70s, plastic rain bonnet, enormous purse) pushes in through the swinging door, shaking water off her arms.

NANA ROSALIND
Nobody told me the pool was closed. I swam in the lobby for ten minutes.

DESMOND
You didn't.

NANA ROSALIND
Figuratively.

Beatrix pours her a coffee. Nana Rosalind sits, takes Pippa's lone flip-flop, and studies it.

NANA ROSALIND (CONT'D)
Where's the other one?

PIPPA
Lost.

A crackle from the wall speaker.

LIFEGUARD (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Attention. Someone's goldfish is in the deep end. In a bag. Please claim it.

Pippa slides off her stool.

PIPPA
Mine.

BEATRIX
You brought a fish to the pool?

PIPPA
He wanted to swim.

DESMOND
It was a good idea, actually.

Beatrix looks at him, then laughs, helpless. Nana Rosalind pats her hand.

NANA ROSALIND
Go get the fish, Beatrix. I'll watch the counter.

A teenager, KOFI MENSAH (16, lifeguard polo, dripping), leans through the pass-through, holding up a sagging bag with a small orange fish.

KOFI
Whose is this? He seems calm.

PIPPA
That's Mr. Bubbles. He's always calm.

Kofi hands the bag over. Pippa cradles it like an egg.

BEATRIX
Thank you, Kofi. I'm so sorry.

KOFI
It's the most exciting thing today.

Rain softens on the skylight. Everyone watches the fish circle once, then settle.
